    ...sec(r'what it asks cargo, and what it never hard-codes'),
    ...text(r'The edition in a new workspace is not written into the plugin. The first time you create a workspace in a session, a throwaway cargo new runs in a temporary directory and the edition is read back from the Cargo.toml cargo wrote. The resolver follows from that: 3 for edition 2024 and newer, 2 before. A plugin with a hard-coded edition is wrong the day cargo moves on; this one is wrong only if cargo’s own output changes shape, and then it says so and stops.'),
    ...code('lua', r'lua/xyno_new/rust.lua · lines 79-82', r'''
--- The resolver that goes with an edition: "3" for 2024 and newer, else "2".
function M.resolver(edition)
