    ...sec(r'how it is tested'),
    ...text(r'nvim -l tests/run.lua runs every spec in its own headless Neovim child process and sums the RESULT lines. The Rust specs run the installed cargo for real in temporary directories (cargo new works offline), and replace it with a shell stub on PATH to test failure: a cargo that exits 101, a cargo that rewrites the edition to 2021 or 2018, a PATH with no cargo at all. The egui specs build a fake eframe_template ZIP with Python and serve it from file:// or from a tiny HTTP server inside the test Neovim, so ETag, If-None-Match and the offline cache are exercised without the network. One test uses the real template and skips without network.'),
